#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148780 :tutorial/content "If we want to find the ratio of two numbers as a percentage, we can use the relationship between multiplication and division.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's determine the missing number below.\n\n![](images/df/dfa98ca128e85d05689ed37be0f29dcc2f1f06ae5ee7c930d5ccc76c2564a736.svg)\n\nWe can interpret the word \"of\" as multiplication:\n![](images/c5/c5002766655275462fbd346ee2dfba78b1ec4b5e2a603e0e38a2d44f19708cfd.svg)\n\nNow, using the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as follows:\n![](images/72/72bd81d10d8c50b1ca5d8a9196585d3da7a5d740fd4c75a86e5cd45a87093495.svg)\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7}{10} = \\dfrac{7 \\times 10}{10 \\times 10} = \\dfrac{70}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{70}{100} = 70\\%\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n70 \\% \\,\\,\\text{of}\\,\\, 10 = 7.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "41806a6e-def6-586b-a059-4450f0974244" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8169 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
